  "note": [
   "The proclamation was read as George Stanley's book reprints it. It says only that the leaf is a single red maple leaf. Canadian Heritage calls it the stylized 11-point leaf and gives the 32 x 64 grid, which isn't law.",
   "The leaf's outline is the path of the Commons file named above, copied without change, and isn't from the law. Canadian Heritage's own leaf files weren't reachable to compare.",
   "The Manufacturing Standards Act leaves manufacture to the CGSB standards CAN/CGSB-98.1, .2 and .3, which weren't read. They'd be the place to look for an official red.",
   "The hex, Pantone and CMYK values are the Album des Pavillons 2023, as reported by FOTW. The Album itself wasn't read. FOTW's other sources give PMS 032 for the flag, and PMS 485 for screens."
  ],
